1. Scope and definitions

This license covers the Aero source code, executable software, documentation,
and runtime components supplied under this license (the "Software"). Each
copyright holder grants rights only to material that holder is authorized to
license. Separately licensed components retain their own terms.

"You" means the person or organization exercising the rights in this license.
When acting for an employer or client, that employer or client is the user for
purposes of eligibility; an individual's personal eligibility does not exempt
an otherwise ineligible organization.

"Commercial Use" means use in operating a business, providing a paid service,
developing or supplying a commercial product, or otherwise pursuing commercial
advantage. It includes using the Aero application or command-line tool inside
a business, whether or not Aero is modified, embedded, or redistributed.

"Independent Developer" means an individual working independently or a
developer-owned and developer-operated business that is not owned or controlled
by another business. Incorporation alone does not disqualify an independent
developer. Work performed on behalf of another organization is assessed under
that organization's eligibility.

"Product" means a product or service incorporating the Software, including its
editions and substantially equivalent offerings. Related offerings may not be
artificially split to avoid the revenue threshold.

"Annual Product Revenue" means gross revenue attributable to that Product
during the preceding twelve months, including sales, subscriptions, licensing,
advertising, and paid services sold as part of the Product, less refunds and
sales taxes collected for a government. It is measured across all distributors
and controlled entities supplying the Product. Unrelated products, personal
income, company valuation, and investment funding are not counted. Amounts are
measured in United States dollars; other currencies are converted at the
exchange rate applicable when the revenue was received.

2. Free-use permissions

Subject to this license, you may obtain, inspect, build, run, copy, modify, and
distribute the Software and your modifications without paying a license fee:

  a. for personal, noncommercial purposes; or

  b. as an Independent Developer, for a Product whose Annual Product Revenue
     is less than USD 1,000,000. This includes using Aero to develop, test,
     operate, and distribute that qualifying Product.

An Independent Developer may develop a new Product under paragraph (b) before
it earns revenue. Eligibility is evaluated separately for each Product. Free
eligibility for one Product does not authorize use for an ineligible Product or
for unrelated commercial operations.

You may also inspect, build, test, and modify Aero solely to evaluate whether to
obtain a commercial license, or to prepare an unpaid contribution to Aero. This
permission does not authorize production use, paid customer services, or other
commercial operation of the Software.

The permission to distribute includes source and executable forms. Recipients
receive their rights directly under this license and must qualify for their
own use. Your eligibility does not exempt your customers, employers, clients,
or other recipients from the commercial licensing requirement.

3. Paid commercial license

Commercial Use outside the Independent Developer exception requires a separate
paid commercial license from the applicable copyright holder or its authorized
licensing representative before that use begins. This requirement applies to
the Aero application, command-line tool, source code, and embedded runtime alike;
there is no separate company-size exemption.

At USD 1,000,000 or more in Annual Product Revenue, the Independent Developer
exception no longer applies to that Product. Obtain a paid commercial license
or stop the affected Commercial Use. Reaching the threshold does not create
retroactive fees for earlier use that qualified under section 2.

Fees, payment arrangements, and additional commercial permissions are established
by the separate commercial agreement. This license sets no automatic fee and
does not itself constitute a paid commercial license. Contact Aero's publisher
through its official project channel to arrange commercial licensing.

4. Visible acknowledgment

If you distribute or publicly offer a product or service incorporating the
Software, make its use of Aero easy for an ordinary user to spot. A statement
such as "Uses Aero" or "Powered by Aero" is sufficient.

Placement and format are flexible. For example, the acknowledgment may appear
in a readily accessible product page, documentation overview, normal application
information screen, or another similarly visible location. No dedicated credits
section, dependency list, splash screen, startup message, or logo is required.

An acknowledgment buried solely in source code, obscure legal files, or an
otherwise difficult-to-find location is insufficient. An unmodified Aero
distribution whose normal presentation already clearly identifies it as Aero
satisfies this acknowledgment requirement.

Merely running an unrelated program with Aero does not require adding an Aero
acknowledgment to that program. Incorporating Aero code or runtime components
into a distributed program does require acknowledgment. A commercial license
changes this requirement only if it expressly says so.

5. Copies, modifications, and output

Include this license with copies of the Software that you distribute. Retain
applicable copyright and license notices. Identify modified distributions as
modified; do not misrepresent them as official Aero releases. You may choose
terms for your own original additions, but those terms must not remove the
conditions applying to Aero material or purport to grant rights you do not hold.

This license does not require publication of your own source code or private
modifications. It does not grant ownership of, or impose Aero licensing terms
on, guest programs, guest operating systems, user data, or other independent
material merely processed by Aero.

Generated or translated output that includes Aero code or runtime components
remains subject to this license for those components. Independent portions of
that output retain their existing rights and licenses. Output containing no
Aero material is not covered solely because Aero produced it.

